{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Deploy the supplied PostgreSQL schema and records as branch_stock on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"PostgreSQL 16 was installed on node1, branch_stock contains both supplied tables, and the final values exactly match the source SQL: stock PAPER=40 and LABELS=18; supplier_costs PAPER=3.25 and LABELS=1.75.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cde873f943a44229","cmd-a8e75377fc04465a","cmd-dcb74a574f604b22","cmd-6db752ec03d94ec7"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Allow stock_app from node2 to read stock and update quantity, while preventing schema changes, non-quantity stock updates, and access to supplier_costs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct node2 tests show stock reads and a rolled-back quantity update succeed, while supplier_costs reads, CREATE TABLE, and SKU updates are denied. The final privilege matrix independently confirms only stock SELECT and quantity-column UPDATE, with no schema CREATE or supplier_costs SELECT privilege.","evidence_ids":["cmd-746368a0159b4a90","cmd-6db752ec03d94ec7","cmd-e4de5c08c9724b1f"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Give auditor read-only access to stock and supplier_costs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Auditor successfully reads joined data from both tables, while an UPDATE is denied. The final privilege matrix confirms SELECT on both tables and no quantity or SKU update privilege.","evidence_ids":["cmd-746368a0159b4a90","cmd-6db752ec03d94ec7","cmd-e4de5c08c9724b1f"]},{"id":"req-4","requirement":"Establish separate credentials for stock_app and auditor on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 has separate root-owned, mode-600 pgpass files. Both roles are login roles with passwords, and PostgreSQL reports their stored password verifiers as distinct. The credentials continued working after node2 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-17d97c83a3f04050","cmd-dcb74a574f604b22","cmd-6e82b8853b184a94","cmd-e4de5c08c9724b1f"]},{"id":"req-5","requirement":"Preserve the supplied records in /srv/l